      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village emerged as one of Noble County's earliest settlements, with Irish pioneers arriving between 1812‑1820.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/summerfield_ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1817 Moses Horton built a cabin and store trading ammunition and tea, sparking a Protestant Irish community that thrived.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/summerfield_ohio",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Underground Railroad activity and anti‑slavery debates took place in Summerfield schoolhouses during the 1830s and 1840s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
